Got it.  There are many ways to do this.  Since your polygon is already an sf object I'll assume you're using sf to do spatial things - I'm assuming you've got both objects using the same coordinate system or crs:

poly <- #your.polygon.feature

points <- st_as_sf(SSdf[[1]], coords = c("X","Y"), crs=#your.crs.from.poly)
in.poly <- unlist(st_intersects(poly,points)) #will return a vector of the rows in the original data frame that are within the polygon(s) in poly
lassicSS[[1]][(in.poly,]

one could do this in less steps, I'm sure, that's just the hack that comes to mind.

Best,
Dan

